well rhiannon mills is outside  parliament for us right now and um  you could sort of see on prince  charles's face i think as he as he  delivered those lines actually i i  wonder if he wonders whether the queen  will be able to attend these events  she's clearly looking forward to them  but as we see the monarchy is flexing  and other people are coming in to assist  her  at the moment as her mobility falters  i think today was was again a reminder  of how  over the years we have become so used to  her majesty the queen  carrying out her public services and  duties  and enjoying relatively good health and  yet now we have a monarch who herself  has admitted in recent weeks and months  that she is having  trouble standing and walking and  as a result of that the royal family the  palace and also the public are going to  have to get used to seeing younger mems  the royal family increasingly stepping  up and taking on some of her  responsibilities and i think yes we will  see that around the platinum jubilee  weekend but if we look at today it was a  hugely  symbolic moment and i think it will be  seen as one of those  defining moments for the monarchy when  historians look back at these twilight  years of this elizabethan age there has  been this softly softly approach to  transition and yes we have seen younger  members of the royal family already  stepping up and helping the queen things  like prince charles laying her wreath at  the cenotaph for remembrance sunday  other mem's royal family carrying out  investitures and also doing those  overseas tours on her behalf but today  was the first time that really we've  seen younger members of the family  taking on what is a key part of her  constitutional role and the decision for  that will not have been taken lightly  literally until the 11th hour we were  told that the queen herself wanted to  come she planned to come but as i think  we've seen in recent weeks when it's  come to things like the commonwealth day  service the maundy service events where  she would have to walk great distances  or sit for a long time and this again  would have been one of them  practicalities simply had to kick in and  that's what's happened  with this one and it was always going to  be interesting for constitutional  experts and the like likes of you and i  to see exactly how the queen wanted this  to play out and i think  those constitutional experts some of  them were  puzzled and surprised by the fact that  she decided to use that letter's patent  so that  change in the rules  to mean that two councillors of state so  her son and grandson would carry out the  responsibilities today but that  ultimately is the way that she decided  it should be and we are seeing the  constitution flex and change  to deal with an ageing monarch although  the palace very keen to point out that  this is not a monarch who is looking at  abdicating if you look at her accession  day speech that she made her accession  day message that she delivered  in february this year to start the  platinum jubilee year once again she  reaffirmed her commitment to serving her  country and the commonwealth but today  she has handed over  maybe just for this year we're going to  have to wait and see but that important  constitutional role of making sure that  the parliamentary session could still  get underway despite the fact that she  wasn't able to appear  here in person but yeah the palace very  clearly also saying that yes she's  having trouble with her mobility but it  is still going to be the queen who will  have a virtual session with privy  council this week it's still going to be  the queen who is going to speak to her  prime minister and ultimately it was her  son and her grandson who were jointly  opening parliament today however i think  the problem is and for those who talk  about this being a regency a prince  regent situation and everything but name  the optics today seeing prince charles  front and center  it did look more like a regency  situation than i suspect the palace  wouldn't necessarily want to but  ultimately that was how the ceremony  played out and the palace stressing that  she is still very much in charge and  certainly when it comes to platinum  jubilee  she will still be the star of  proceedings  okay rhiannon thank you very much
 

